  "2026-07-11T23:15:35.696Z",codex-root,"Progress evidence: implemented and SDK-exported an idempotent fenced .gitignore primitive; pm init applies it in workspace-discovery, explicit workspace, and .agents/pm tracker-path layouts; repair/idempotence/unit/integration and packed-consumer proof pass. Remaining acceptance work: add health/validate detection for already-tracked cache files before closing."
  "2026-07-23T20:35:24.737Z",claude-code-agent,"GitHub intake update (2026-07-23): issue #659 reports the remaining custom --pm-path runtime-cache ignore gap. This is the same canonical lineage as GH #514, with the earlier custom-root bootstrap portion already completed by pm-4uqm. Reusing pm-hous rather than creating a duplicate; the remaining acceptance still covers health/validate detection and runtime-cache ignore ownership."
  "2026-07-24T12:05:49.068Z",claude-code-agent,"Read-only-intent dogfood finding: running pm init --agent-guidance status on current main rewrote the managed .gitignore block by adding the checkpoints path even though the requested subaction was status. The workspace change was reverted after inspection. This belongs to the existing init-owned ignore lineage here: status/reporting paths should not mutate repository files, while explicit init/repair paths remain idempotent owners of the canonical block."
  "2026-07-24T12:40:40.080Z",codex-root-agent,"Implementation start: claimed as an actively worked part of the broad SDK workspace mutation integrity PR. TDD scope covers deterministic id allocation, atomic stale-lock takeover, init cache and merge-fence ownership, schema migration idempotency/recovery, cross-runtime machine channels, and the fixed 10k performance gate."
  "2026-07-24T13:27:13.738Z",codex-root-agent,"Implementation evidence: health.integrity and validate.storage_integrity now share a read-only Git index scan covering runtime/, search/, locks/, transactions/, and checkpoints/ under default or custom tracker roots. Findings contain repository-relative paths and an exact index-only git rm --cached remediation, while non-Git workspaces remain clean. Focused functional suite passed: 3 files, 147 tests. Repo lint/static quality/docstring gate and typecheck pass. The attempted focused coverage command correctly failed the repository-wide 100% threshold because it intentionally ran only 3 of 354 files; the authoritative full coverage gate will be rerun after the packed acceptance proof."
  "2026-07-24T13:34:59.340Z",codex-root-agent,"Completion evidence: final packed package detected one force-indexed runtime artifact through both health and validate, emitted exactly git rm --cached -r -- '.agents/pm/runtime', preserved the local cache after applying the remediation, and cleared the validation warning. The shared scan covers runtime/search/locks/transactions/checkpoints, custom roots, non-Git workspaces, compact health projections, and exact fix hints. Final full gate: 355 files, 6220 tests, 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-07-24T13:37:24.886Z",codex-root-agent,"Acceptance refinement from self-dogfood: the first live scan correctly surfaced the repository's intentional .agents/pm/search/eval-queries.json corpus. That file is authoritative relevance ground truth, not derived cache state, so the scanner now explicitly excludes it while retaining detection for every other indexed search artifact. Focused regression and live health/validate both pass with zero warnings."
